    thinking: "**Defining the Scope**\n\nI\'m solidifying the project\'s parameters. \"Kapas Ki Sehat,\" the Android app, is taking shape as a 3-screen prototype. The design will be \"Executive Tech,\" using the dark theme and mint-green accents specified. My initial understanding is now concrete: I\'m focused on this app\'s fundamental structure and visual style, as the user described it.\n\n\n**Refining the Details**\n\nI\'m now diving into the specifics: Kotlin and Jetpack Compose are the chosen tools. I\'ve mapped the architecture: Home, Scanner, Result, and back to Home. The \"Executive Tech\" theme is refined with the requested colors and rounded corners. Bilingual strings are planned; I\'ll hardcode those for now. I\'ve updated the metadata.json, and the application ID, and I think I\'ll need Navigation Compose.\n\n\n**Evaluating Skill Priorities**\n\nI\'m now assessing skill relevance. I\'ve decided to hold off on `android-secret-management` since we\'re mocking the AI. Although I might consider app icon generation later, my priority is the core functionality and polished UI: I\'m examining `frontend-design` and `app-icon-generation` skills and guidelines, and I must not skip the app icon!\n\n\n"
