  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Uncovering Dependencies**\n\nI\'ve hit a snag with `view_file` for `libs.versions.toml`, but I\'ve located commented dependencies within `app/build.gradle.kts`. It looks like `libs.androidx.navigation.compose` is readily available, so it\'s a simple uncomment! Additionally, the `applicationId` will need updating.\n\n\n**Clarifying Persistence Needs**\n\nI\'m reassessing the need for Room. Initial thoughts considered its use for \"Save to log,\" but given the prototype scope and explicit AI simulation, data persistence seems unnecessary. I\'ll maintain a mocked approach and state clearing if no actual data tracking is required for the log, and I\'ll confirm with you, as the expert. I\'m focusing on the three requested screens: Home, Scanner, and Result.\n\n\n**Orchestrating Configuration Changes**\n\nI\'m now focusing on a flurry of file modifications: `metadata.json`, `app/build.gradle.kts`, `strings.xml`, `Theme.kt`, and `Color.kt`. I\'m also including `MainActivity.kt`. It\'s mandatory to create an app icon, so I\'m using `generate_image` in parallel with this, targeting \"cotton_scan_icon\" with the prompt: \"Bold, flat vector silhouette of a cotton leaf inside a sleek digital scanner viewfinder square.\" I\'m also ensuring `androidx.compose.material.icons.extended` is uncommented, as it might be needed.\n\n\n**Refining Aesthetic & Configuration**\n\nI\'m now implementing the design details. I\'ve updated `metadata.json` with a project name, description, and retaining the major capability. I also adjusted the `applicationId` in `build.gradle.kts`. Plus, I uncommented `libs.androidx.navigation.compose`. I have a clear vision: a minimalist, professional look with a charcoal background and mint green accents. I\'m focusing on the structural build.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 12
      nanos: 344773349
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
