  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Applying Design to Android**\n\nI\'m now integrating the \"Professional Polish\" theme into the `MainActivity.kt` Android app for \"Kapas Ki Sehat.\" Initial steps focus on the HTML background color, which is a charcoal black `#121212`, and the Header text color, as specified in the HTML. I am now proceeding to other elements in the design.\n\n\n**Implementing UI Elements**\n\nNow, I\'m focusing on the specifics for the UI components within the app. I\'m taking the styling directly from the design HTML. The \"Agri-Tech v2.4\" badge, welcome line with right-aligned Urdu text, and the District Health Card are up next. I\'m paying careful attention to colors like `#e5c07b` for the header and the grid layout for temperature, humidity, and wind. I\'m also preparing to create the Critical Risk section and the Hero Button, focusing on rounded corners and specific colors. Lastly, I\'ll incorporate the bottom navigation bar.\n\n\n**Refining UI Components**\n\nI\'m now carefully translating the HTML header into composable elements. I\'m focusing on the `Kapas Ki Sehat` title with the specific yellow color (`#e5c07b`) and the \"Agri-Tech v2.4\" badge, keeping a close eye on the font styles and tracking. Next, I\'ll tackle the cloud sync indicator, ensuring the green dot and text align perfectly with the HTML design\'s intention. I\'m working to recreate the visual styles through Compose.\n\n\n**Recreating UI Elements**\n\nI\'m now implementing the detailed design specifications in code. I\'ve focused on the text styles for the app\'s header, using bold wheat-gold for the main title and monospace, semi-transparent text for the badge. I\'ve also implemented the cloud sync indicator, mirroring the HTML design\'s green dot and active text within a circular surface with the correct border. I am carefully translating the design elements into composable UI components.\n\n\n**Translating Right-Aligned Text**\n\nI\'m currently working to integrate the right-aligned, dual-language welcome message into the app\'s `MainActivity.kt`. I\'m using a `Column` composable to arrange the English and Urdu text. I\'ve set the font weights and colors as specified, and I\'m ensuring the Urdu text aligns to the right using `textAlign = TextAlign.End`. This includes adjusting font sizes to be appropriate, and the styling mirrors the original HTML design for a seamless user experience. I\'m taking care to correctly implement the Urdu text, so it is presented in the correct form.\n\n\n**Constructing Card UI Elements**\n\nI\'m now focused on the District Health & Risk card. I\'ve successfully created the basic structure using `Surface` with rounded corners and a border. I am now working on placing the text elements, including \"DISTRICT HEALTH & RISK\" with wheat-gold color and the \"Multan Belt\" badge, within the card, and am using a `Row` and a nested `Surface` with `RoundedCornerShape` to replicate the specified design. I\'m carefully translating the styling into Jetpack Compose.\n\n\n**Implementing Card Data**\n\nI\'m now integrating the data elements within the health card, focusing on a temperature display and weather information. I\'ve set up a row to arrange the data, including a temperature icon and numerical value with the respective styling, followed by the weather condition text below. I\'m leveraging `Box` composables for layout, including `padding` and `color` settings, and aligning the items in the proper format. I\'m focusing on ensuring these pieces align to the original design.\n\n\n**Adding Weather Elements**\n\nI\'m now integrating the humidity and wind components into the weather data display within the District Health & Risk card. I\'m leveraging `Box` composables with `RoundedCornerShape` and appropriate `padding` to recreate the desired visual style. I\'m focusing on the correct font size, weight, and color, along with icon placement for the humidity element. The background color has been set to `#F8FAFC`. I\'m working to make sure these elements align to the existing design.\n\n\n\n**Adding Wind Speed**\n\nI\'m now integrating the wind speed component within the weather data section of the District Health & Risk card. I\'ve used a `Box` composable with `RoundedCornerShape` and padding to recreate the visual style. I\'m focusing on the correct icon, the wind speed value, and the corresponding \"WIND SPEED\" label, ensuring proper font styles and alignment. The background is set, and I\'m ensuring all the components are aligned according to the design.\n\n\n**Constructing Risk Section**\n\nI am now structuring the critical risk section. I am building a composable for \"High Risk\" and its Urdu translation, with specific colors and styles. I am ensuring that the Urdu text correctly aligns to the end of the screen, and I\'m ensuring that all the text elements use the right spacing and line height. I\'m focusing on text color and formatting to match the HTML design. I\'m also ensuring the text is correct, based on the data.\n\n\n\n**Building Scan Button**\n\nI\'m now implementing the scan button, crafting it as a composable element within the app. I\'m focusing on the visual styling: a circular surface with a camera icon and text elements beneath, all properly styled. I\'m using appropriate spacing and colors for both English and Urdu text. I\'m focusing on ensuring proper text size and font weight for a seamless experience. The button will be incorporated in the bottom navigation.\n\n\n**Designing Bottom Navigation**\n\nI\'m now building the bottom navigation bar with Jetpack Compose, focusing on the visual styles specified in the design. I\'m starting with the home button, including its green dot indicator, icon, and uppercase text. I\'m focusing on making the home button active. Next, I\'ll build the history button, focusing on opacity. I\'m carefully translating the styling into code.\n\n\n**Finalizing Bottom Navigation**\n\nI\'ve completed the bottom navigation bar by adding the history and profile buttons. I\'ve focused on styling the history and profile buttons correctly, including opacity adjustments, to reflect their inactive state as specified in the design. I\'ve also finalized positioning to ensure correct placement.\n\n\n**Choosing Button Implementation**\n\nI\'m now deciding on the best method for the hero button implementation. After evaluating options like `Surface` with `onClick`, `Box` with `clickable`, and `Card`, I\'ve decided to proceed with the `Card` component for optimal flexibility and design coherence. I am planning to implement the `onClick` functionality and style parameters.\n\n\n**Replacing HomeScreen**\n\nI\'m now rewriting the `HomeScreen` in `MainActivity.kt`, focusing on a `Scaffold` layout with a `Column` for content, inside of padding for the padding parameters. I have built the Header and am proceeding to translate the design for the content areas within the app. I have just replaced the `HomeScreen` implementation block in code with the above plan.\n\n\n**Integrating Welcome Message**\n\nI am now focusing on the welcome message, specifically the dual-language implementation within the new design. I\'m using `Column` with `Text` composables for the English and Urdu translations, incorporating padding and applying right alignment for the Urdu text via `TextAlign.End`. I am adjusting font sizes to be suitable, so the welcome message appears as specified in the provided HTML. I will move on to the next section after this is complete.\n\n\n**Constructing Content Area**\n\nI\'m now integrating the District Health Card within the `Column` layout. I\'ve designed the card using a `Surface` with rounded corners and a border. I am incorporating shadow elevation and nested `Column` elements for the card\'s content, and applying padding parameters. I\'m focusing on ensuring it looks correct, according to the HTML design.\n\n\n**Refining Card Layout**\n\nI\'m now carefully implementing the text layout within the District Health & Risk card, using a `Row` composable with `Arrangement.SpaceBetween` for the title and badge. I am focusing on text styling for the District Health and Multan Belt with respective colors and spacing. I\'m ensuring everything aligns exactly according to the provided HTML. I will move on to the next card component.\n\n\n**Adding Card Temperature**\n\nI\'m now integrating the second block of weather data, including humidity and temperature icons and labels, into the card. I\'m leveraging a `Row` composable for arrangement and applying specific background colors, font styles, and icon sizing for each element. The spacing between the icons and labels is carefully defined, and I\'m ensuring everything aligns precisely with the design.\n\n\n**Integrating Wind Speed**\n\nI am now adding the wind speed data into the District Health & Risk card, mirroring the HTML design. I\'m focusing on text and spacing parameters to maintain consistency with the provided design. Specifically, I\'m setting the correct background color and ensuring appropriate padding and text styles for both the wind speed value and the label, for a seamless look.\n\n\n**Implementing Risk Section**\n\nI am now structuring the critical risk section. I\'m building composables for \"CRITICAL WHITEFLY RISK\" and its Urdu translation, focusing on background color, and specific colors and styles for the text. I\'m ensuring the Urdu text is correctly aligned to the end of the screen, with correct spacing and line height. I\'m focused on text color and formatting to match the HTML design. I\'m also ensuring the text is correct, based on the data.\n\n\n**Finalizing Critical Risk**\n\nI\'m now implementing the complete critical risk section, ensuring accurate data display and formatting. I\'m focusing on the \"High risk\" message and its Urdu translation, with specific colors and styles for each element. The Urdu text is set up to align to the end of the screen, and I\'m ensuring there is proper spacing between all the elements. I\'m taking care to correctly implement data.\n\n\n**Constructing Hero Button**\n\nI\'m now building the hero button using a `Box` composable with a `Surface` for the click handling and appearance. I\'ve set the background color and rounded corners. Inside, I\'m integrating a `Column` for content alignment and a nested `Surface` for the circular icon, with shadow and color adjustments to match the HTML design. This includes icon integration and text formatting.\n\n\n**Building Scan Button UI**\n\nI\'m now integrating the scan button into the layout. It\'s built as a `Box` with a nested `Column`. Within the column, I have an image and two text fields in English and Urdu, following the provided HTML\'s styling and layout guidelines. I\'m focusing on the circular icon\'s size and tint, as well as text sizes and colors. The circular surface contains an image and text. I\'m taking care to ensure the text is correct, based on the data.\n\n\n**Refining Bottom Navigation Style**\n\nI\'m now refining the bottom navigation bar to perfectly match the design. I\'ve focused on styling the home button, including the green dot indicator, and text styling for the history and profile buttons. I\'ve also incorporated the correct opacity adjustments for the inactive states. Next, I\'ll integrate the History and Profile buttons.\n\n\n\n**Refining Button Styles**\n\nI\'m now implementing the history and expert (profile) buttons, making sure to apply the correct styles to match the HTML design. I\'m carefully translating the opacity and letter spacing, focusing on the icon sizes and text colors. I\'ve finished the bottom navigation bar and will move on to the next component.\n\n\n"
