    thinking: "**Implementing Urdu Typography**\n\nI\'m currently integrating the `UrduTypography` style. I\'ve successfully imported the necessary `Font` and defined the `UrduFontFamily` using `jameel_noori_nastaleeq`. Now, I\'m defining the `UrduTypography` with the designated font family, establishing the stylistic foundation for Urdu text rendering.\n\n\n**Addressing Font Handling**\n\nI\'ve realized a potential runtime issue with the font implementation. Specifically, if the XML font resource is empty, the `Font` constructor in Compose could throw an exception when it tries to read it. I\'m considering using `FontFamily.Default` as a safe fallback or adding a try-catch block for resilience. I\'m also exploring if the Android framework provides a built-in fallback mechanism for missing fonts to avoid a hard crash. I am trying to adhere to the mapping requirements.\n\n\n**Refining Font Loading**\n\nI\'m now focusing on a robust solution for font loading. I\'ve encountered potential crash points if `jameel_noori_nastaleeq.xml` is missing or invalid. I\'m leaning toward employing a `try-catch` block for fault tolerance during font instantiation. The current approach involves using `FontFamily.Default` as a safe fallback and I\'ve also constructed a minimal XML font resource to handle placeholder scenarios for a more resilient implementation. I am trying to resolve the crash potential. I\'m assigning `FontFamily.Default` and commenting out the `Font`.\n\n\n**Considering Font Substitution**\n\nI\'m now contemplating how to handle the placeholder font. The environment might inject a real `.ttf` later, so I\'ll create a dummy or keep the `jameel_noori_nastaleeq.xml` empty. I\'m exploring the crash risk if `Font(R.font.jameel_noori_nastaleeq)` is used directly with a missing font, and the cleanest method of mapping. It appears that `FontFamily.Default` can be combined to achieve this. The previous approach was flawed, but I have a direction now.\n\n\n**Mapping Font Logic**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing the clean mapping of the placeholder font, aiming for a seamless display. If the font file, like `jameel_noori_nastaleeq.ttf`, is missing, I\'ll default to the system font for rendering. This aligns with the placeholder strategy. I\'m implementing a `try-catch` block around the font instantiation, switching to `FontFamily.Default` if an exception occurs during the mapping. I\'m attempting to resolve it gracefully.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 15
      nanos: 414842428
    }
