  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Investigating Font Loading Failure**\n\nI\'ve traced a crash to an empty font file, `jameel_noori_nastaleeq.ttf`, triggering an `IllegalStateException` during Jetpack Compose\'s typeface resolution. I believe the file\'s emptiness stemmed from a previous attempt where I created it as an XML layout. I\'m focusing on why an empty font file even exists on the file system and how to prevent it. I\'m now trying to recreate the file and process to understand the bug, and am now looking at how to safely create or delete font files.\n\n\n**Resolving Font Loading Issue**\n\nI\'ve determined the core problem: the empty `.ttf` file. An invalid file results in an `IllegalStateException` during typeface resolution in Jetpack Compose. I\'m thinking I should remove the invalid `.ttf` reference and fallback, maybe using `FontFamily.Default`, to avoid a crash during rendering. I\'ll update `Type.kt` so it doesn\'t even attempt to load it from `R.font`. The `Font(...)` call might not throw in the try-catch, because the actual crash seems to be when the font is resolved during measure/render.\n\n\n**Refining Font Loading Strategy**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on a cleaner approach. Instead of attempting a fallback, I\'m leaning toward eliminating the problematic font reference altogether. I\'m removing the empty `.ttf` file. This means I\'ll remove `R.font.jameel_noori_nastaleeq` and use `FontFamily.Default` in `Type.kt`. This eliminates the crash directly without complex fallbacks. The goal is a more robust solution that keeps it simple.\n\n\n"
