    items {
      text: "\"The layout is stable now, but the Urdu typography is still falling back to the default Arabic Naskh font system. Let\'s fix this cleanly for the presentation without using local asset file references.\n\nIn your global theme configuration, inject a custom font provider or download link to fetch a verified Jameel Noori Nastaleeq web font dynamically at runtime.\n\nIf dynamic font loading is restricted by the workspace emulator, modify the CSS/styling layer of the Android rendering frame to inject a custom @font-face rule pointing to a public repository hosting the \'Jameel Noori Nastaliq\' .ttf or .woff2 file.\n\nForce-apply this downloaded font family explicitly to the TextStyle of the main welcome header and the \'SCAN CROP\' Urdu text.\n\nEnsure the lineHeight for these text components remains augmented so the script loops do not clip inside the mint-green action button.\""
