  user_input {
    user_response: "We have successfully deployed the app to a physical test device (LM-V405), but we need to resolve a few layout scaling bugs and handle hardware fallback states cleanly. Please modify the Jetpack Compose code with the following fixes:\n\n1. FIX ACTION BUTTON PADDING & CLIPPING (HERO BUTTON):\n   * Wrap the entire main content column of the Home Dashboard in a proper \'Modifier.statusBarsPadding()\' and \'Modifier.navigationBarsPadding()\'. This will prevent the top elements from clipping into the system status bar.\n   * Add explicit \'Modifier.padding(bottom = 16.dp)\' to the bottom navigation bar area so the navigation buttons do not sit too close to the Android system software keys.\n   * On the massive mint-green \'SCAN CROP\' button, adjust the internal column constraints: place the camera icon at the top, followed by \'SCAN CROP\' (English), and then \'\332\251\331\276\330\247\330\263 \332\251\330\247 \331\276\330\252\333\201 \330\247\330\263\332\251\333\214\331\206 \332\251\330\261\333\214\332\272\' (Urdu) below it. Add defensive vertical padding inside the button container to guarantee the Urdu text is fully visible and never cut off by the button\'s bottom edge.\n\n2. IMPLEMENT A SECURE CAMERA VIEW FALLBACK:\n   * Since the backend ML pipeline is not yet linked to the native CameraX preview stream, implement a clean \'Mock Viewfinder\' fallback state on the device.\n   * Inside the green target box on Screen Two, instead of a solid grey block, display a live, clean placeholder text overlay: \"READY FOR INFERENCE PIPELINE / \332\251\333\214\331\205\330\261\333\201 \330\247\333\214\332\251\331\271\333\214\331\210 \333\201\333\222\" with a subtle, blinking green dot to simulate an active camera feed.\n   * This allows us to explicitly demonstrate the exact layout flow to partners while clearly communicating that the upcoming milestone is the backend model integration."
    items {
      text: "We have successfully deployed the app to a physical test device (LM-V405), but we need to resolve a few layout scaling bugs and handle hardware fallback states cleanly. Please modify the Jetpack Compose code with the following fixes:\n\n1. FIX ACTION BUTTON PADDING & CLIPPING (HERO BUTTON):\n   * Wrap the entire main content column of the Home Dashboard in a proper \'Modifier.statusBarsPadding()\' and \'Modifier.navigationBarsPadding()\'. This will prevent the top elements from clipping into the system status bar.\n   * Add explicit \'Modifier.padding(bottom = 16.dp)\' to the bottom navigation bar area so the navigation buttons do not sit too close to the Android system software keys.\n   * On the massive mint-green \'SCAN CROP\' button, adjust the internal column constraints: place the camera icon at the top, followed by \'SCAN CROP\' (English), and then \'\332\251\331\276\330\247\330\263 \332\251\330\247 \331\276\330\252\333\201 \330\247\330\263\332\251\333\214\331\206 \332\251\330\261\333\214\332\272\' (Urdu) below it. Add defensive vertical padding inside the button container to guarantee the Urdu text is fully visible and never cut off by the button\'s bottom edge.\n\n2. IMPLEMENT A SECURE CAMERA VIEW FALLBACK:\n   * Since the backend ML pipeline is not yet linked to the native CameraX preview stream, implement a clean \'Mock Viewfinder\' fallback state on the device.\n   * Inside the green target box on Screen Two, instead of a solid grey block, display a live, clean placeholder text overlay: \"READY FOR INFERENCE PIPELINE / \332\251\333\214\331\205\330\261\333\201 \330\247\333\214\332\251\331\271\333\214\331\210 \333\201\333\222\" with a subtle, blinking green dot to simulate an active camera feed.\n   * This allows us to explicitly demonstrate the exact layout flow to partners while clearly communicating that the upcoming milestone is the backend model integration."
    }
  }
}
