  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Addressing Layout Issues**\n\nI\'m currently focused on resolving the scaling bugs in the layout, specifically addressing the padding and clipping of the Action Button, or \"Hero Button\", on the home screen. Wrapping the main content in `Modifier.statusBarsPadding()` is a primary fix. This approach will ensure the layout adapts correctly across various devices and orientations. The next steps will involve thorough testing with various hardware fallbacks.\n\n\n**Refining Padding Strategy**\n\nI\'ve shifted my attention to padding, aiming for a cleaner solution. My goal is to apply `navigationBarsPadding()` and `statusBarsPadding()` directly to the `Column` within the `Scaffold`. I\'m verifying this is the best approach to account for both safe drawing insets and edge-to-edge layouts. This is to prevent top elements from clipping into the status bar. The Scaffold\'s padding and potential edge-to-edge configurations need to be considered.\n\n\n**Implementing Bottom Padding**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the bottom navigation bar. I\'m adding `Modifier.padding(bottom = 16.dp)` to the `BottomNavBar` composable to ensure visual consistency and spacing. I\'m also addressing the layout of the \"SCAN CROP\" button, adding internal column constraints and padding to properly arrange its elements, including the camera icon, text labels, and the Urdu translation, ensuring proper vertical spacing.\n\n**Building Camera Fallback**\n\nI\'ve moved on to Task 2, the secure camera view fallback. I\'m replacing the solid gray block in the ScannerScreen\'s green target box with placeholder text: \"READY FOR INFERENCE PIPELINE / \332\251\333\214\331\205\330\261\333\201 \330\247\333\214\332\251\331\271\333\214\331\210 \333\201\333\222\". I\'ll center this text within the cutout area of the existing `Canvas` using a simple `InfiniteTransition` for the blinking green dot effect to mimic an active camera. I\'ll be modifying `MainActivity.kt` next.\n\n\n**Verifying Scaffold Padding**\n\nI\'m now back on the home screen layout. I\'m taking a close look at the `Column` modifier. I\'m checking if the `Scaffold`\'s `innerPadding` already accounts for system bar padding. I want to avoid double-padding the content. I\'ve added `statusBarsPadding()` and `navigationBarsPadding()` to the home screen `Column`, and added `padding(top = 16.dp)` to the `BottomNavBar` composable. I\'m verifying that the scaffold setup doesn\'t conflict with these additions.\n\n\n**Adding Bottom Padding**\n\nI\'ve added bottom padding of 16dp to the home screen\'s main content area, specifically to the column. Also, I\'ve added padding to the Scan Crop button\'s internal column with a top and bottom padding of 24dp for better visual spacing of its children and components.\n\n\n**Refining Button Layout**\n\nI\'m now refining the layout of the \"SCAN CROP\" button\'s internal structure. I\'m focusing on arranging its child elements correctly. I\'ve placed the camera icon at the top, followed by the English text \"SCAN CROP\", and finally the Urdu translation \"\332\251\331\276\330\247\330\263 \332\251\330\247 \331\276\330\252\333\201 \330\247\330\263\332\251\333\214\331\206 \332\251\330\261\333\214\332\272\".\n\n\n**Adjusting Button Padding**\n\nI am now focusing on refining the internal padding of the \"SCAN CROP\" button. I\'ve added vertical and horizontal padding to the inner `Column` that is inside the `Surface` of the button to enhance its visual layout, particularly for the text and icon. I will be adjusting the spacing and padding for the Urdu translation below.\n\nI\'ve also moved to Task 2, which requires a placeholder overlay in the ScannerScreen. Instead of a gray block, I\'ll display the text \"READY FOR INFERENCE PIPELINE / \332\251\333\214\331\205\330\261\333\201 \330\247\333\214\332\251\331\271\333\214\331\210 \333\201\333\222\" with a blinking green dot using `InfiniteTransition`. I\'m going to center the text within the target box.\n\n\n**Implementing Blinking Dot**\n\nI\'m now incorporating a blinking green dot using `InfiniteTransition` within the \"READY FOR INFERENCE PIPELINE\" text placeholder. I\'ve set up an infinite repeatable animation to create the desired visual effect. Additionally, I\'ve implemented a `LaunchedEffect` to simulate the scanning process with a 2-second delay before navigating to the \"diagnosis\" screen, assuming `isScanning` is true.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 13
      nanos: 664815338
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
