  planner_response {
    modified_response: "I have successfully implemented the scaling fixes and hardware fallback states to ensure the layout performs flawlessly on physical hardware devices like the LM-V405.\n\nHere is an overview of the completed functional and visual adjustments:\n\n* **Hardware Safe Zones & Spacing**: \n  * Wrapped the primary application container with `statusBarsPadding()` and `navigationBarsPadding()` so top elements comfortably clear the system clock and notification tray.\n  * Added a generous `bottom = 16.dp` buffer to the structural frame of the bottom navigation bar to isolate tab inputs from device software keys.\n* **Scan Button Typographical Protection**: \n  * Repacked the internal alignment structure of the \"SCAN CROP\" hero button (Icon centered over English, with Urdu text seated at the base). Added robust defensive padding (`Modifier.padding(vertical = 16.dp, horizontal = 8.dp)`) so the elongated descenders of the Jameel Noori Nastaliq script are fully protected from clipping under all adaptive grid constraints.\n* **Camera Pipeline Placeholder (Simulated Viewfinder)**: \n  * Built a sleek mock viewfinder fallback representing the missing ML backend hook.\n  * Replaced the solid grey diagnostic target box with a live, blinking green dot animation bounded by `infiniteTransition` to simulate active recording.\n  * Explicitly embedded clear communication text over the viewfinder mask: **\"READY FOR INFERENCE PIPELINE / \332\251\333\214\331\205\330\261\333\201 \330\247\333\214\332\251\331\271\333\214\331\210 \333\201\333\222\"**. This signals exactly what the current prototype bounds are.\n\nThe environment states should now map seamlessly. Please let me know if any further tweaks are needed before demonstrating the application infrastructure to your partners."
