  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Implementing Contextual Logic**\n\nI\'ve begun integrating the context into the `ScannerScreen` using `LocalContext.current`. My next step is to choose and implement the permission handling, likely leveraging Accompanist for its capabilities, or exploring the standard launcher approach. The goal is to provide a seamless flow in accordance with user permission needs.\n\n\n**Refining Permission Handling**\n\nI\'m now implementing permission handling directly within `ScannerScreen` using `rememberLauncherForActivityResult`. I\'ve implemented a check for camera permissions using `ContextCompat.checkSelfPermission` and, if needed, launched a permission request. I\'ve stored the permission status using `mutableStateOf` to refresh. This provides a clean way to manage permission requests within the composable, only displaying the camera content once permission is granted, and showing a button to re-request if permission is denied.\n\n\n**Optimizing Permission Request Timing**\n\nI\'ve decided launching the permission request immediately within `LaunchedEffect` is the best approach. I\'ve modified `ScannerScreen` to implement the immediate launch. This aligns well with user experience, according to the requirements, and avoids any awkward delays.\n\n\n**Finalizing Scanner Implementation**\n\nI\'ve integrated the `rememberLauncherForActivityResult` with a `LaunchedEffect` to handle camera permission requests. The status updates `hasCameraPermission`. I\'ve also added infinite animation and a scan duration delay. Upon successful scan, the app navigates to the \"diagnosis\" screen and pops up to \"home\".\n\n\n**Displaying Permission Request**\n\nI\'ve just added a UI to handle denied camera permissions within `ScannerScreen`. When camera access is denied, a visually prominent overlay appears. This overlay includes a clear icon and a button that, upon clicking, launches the permission request. I added translations in both English and Urdu. The goal is to make it super clear to the user what they need to do to use the feature.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 13
      nanos: 451099221
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
