sue.\n\n\n**Investigating Certificate Details**\n\nI\'m now diving into the actual certificate content, specifically the base64 string provided: `AyugAwIBAgIJAMLgh0ZkSjCNMA0GCSqGSIb3DQEBBAUAM...`. My goal is to determine if the certificate itself has an error, potentially explaining the parsing failure. I\'m focusing on its structure and data to pinpoint any inconsistencies.\n\n\n**Comparing Certificate Content**\n\nI\'ve shifted my focus to the base64 string provided in the official Google Fonts documentation for Jetpack Compose: `MIIEqDCCA5CgAwIBAgIJANWFuGx90071MA0GCSqGSIb3DQEBBAUAMIGUMQswCQYDVQQGEwJV...`. I\'m going to compare it to the existing certificate data in the `font_certs.xml` file, to see if there is any critical difference. The goal is to identify if the content provided in official documentation, will actually resolve the parse failures.\n\n\n**Verifying Certificate Data**\n\nI\'m now cross-referencing the full base64 certificate provided from `font_certs.xml` with the data available in the Google documentation. The documentation provides a full certificate as a base64 encoded string. I\'m carefully examining the content, character by character, to make sure it matches the details in the file.\n\n\n"
