  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Refining UI Structure**\n\nOkay, I\'m adjusting the UI. My focus is migrating `KapasApp` to use `Scaffold`. I\'m systematically removing redundant `.navigationBarsPadding()` calls from the inner screens, which seem unnecessary now. I\'m also removing `BottomNavBar(...)` calls from the inner screen compositions, aiming to make `BottomNavBar` more generic.\n\n\n**Implementing Scaffold Integration**\n\nI\'ve successfully integrated `Scaffold` into `KapasApp`, improving the overall structure. My current focus is on managing the `BottomNavBar` visibility based on the current route, ensuring it displays only on designated screens. The `paddingValues` are also now correctly passed to `NavHost`. Next, I will be cleaning up all screen compositions and moving navigation logic to parent composables where appropriate.\n\n\n**Integrating Navigation Logic**\n\nI\'m now integrating the navigation logic. I\'ve realized I need `currentBackStackEntryAsState()` from `androidx.navigation.compose`, and, thankfully, `getValue` is already imported. I am currently working on how to properly integrate the navigation logic within the `BottomNavBar` to keep track of the current route. My goal is to dynamically render the navigation bar based on the current screen.\n\n\n**Adjusting NavBar Padding**\n\nI\'m now focusing on padding within the `BottomNavBar`. I was instructed to remove hardcoded bottom padding from individual screen components, and I realize now that `Scaffold.bottomBar` alone doesn\'t automatically handle padding for the `BottomNavBar` custom `Row`. Therefore, I need to include `.navigationBarsPadding()` or `.windowInsetsPadding(WindowInsets.navigationBars)` for proper insets. I will also remove the `padding(bottom = 16.dp)` per instructions, and adjust to `padding(bottom = 8.dp)`.\n\n\n"
