    thinking: "**Defining Urdu Typography**\n\nI\'m currently working on incorporating the Jameel Noori Nastaleeq font within `Type.kt`. My idea is to create a `FontFamily` object and use it to define a `TextStyle` for Urdu text. I\'m exploring the integration of this with `androidx.compose`.\n\n\n**Addressing Font Fallbacks**\n\nI\'ve hit a snag with font fallbacks in my Urdu typography implementation. Specifically, if the `GoogleFont` fails to load, I can\'t easily integrate `FontFamily.Serif` as a fallback within the `FontFamily` definition. I was hoping to leverage `FontFamily(Font(...))` but it seems direct system font fallback isn\'t straightforward. Using `FontFamily.Serif` within a try-catch is cumbersome for dynamic loading. I\'m reviewing the documentation again for any alternative strategies, and just noted I can use another `Font` for fallback.\n\n\n**Refining Font Fallback Strategy**\n\nI\'m making progress. I realized I can utilize the `FontFamily(List<Font>)` constructor in Compose 1.3. This approach allows me to specify a Google Font and a local fallback font. My revised plan involves creating a `FontFamily` with the Google Font as the primary, and `Font(resId = R.font.serif)` as the secondary, ensuring a fallback to a serif font if the Google Font fails. This will directly address the download delay concern and improve readability during font loading.\n\n\n**Investigating Fallback Options**\n\nI\'m now diving deeper into how to handle font loading and fallbacks. I was considering keeping the `fontFamily` as the Google Font, but the prompt asks for a fallback during delays. I\'ve been considering `FontLoadingStrategy.Async`, and I just realized I can\'t directly define a `fallbackFontFamily` in `TextStyle`. I\'m now exploring if I can integrate `FontFamily.Serif` as a secondary font within the `FontFamily` itself. It looks like it won\'t work that way.\n\n\n**Exploring Font Fallbacks**\n\nI\'ve hit a conceptual roadblock. It seems I can\'t directly use system `FontFamily` instances as fallbacks within a custom `FontFamily` in Compose. This realization has shifted my approach. It looks like it won\'t be possible to use it in `Type.kt`. The user might be expecting something technically impossible. I\'m now exploring if I can integrate `FontFamily.Serif` as a secondary font within the `FontFamily` itself, but that isn\'t working as I had hoped. I\'ll just change the text style to `JameelNooriNastaleeq` and move on.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 11
      nanos: 171788165
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
