    user_response: "Please update my Jetpack Compose project to replace the simulated mock camera feed with a real live camera feed using CameraX. \n\n1. DEPENDENCIES: \nOpen `app/build.gradle.kts` and add the following CameraX libraries to the dependencies block. Sync the project afterward:\nimplementation(\"androidx.camera:camera-camera2:1.3.1\")\nimplementation(\"androidx.camera:camera-lifecycle:1.3.1\")\nimplementation(\"androidx.camera:camera-view:1.3.1\")\n\n2. UI REFACTOR: \nIn my UI code, locate the `ScannerScreen` composable. Find the mock camera base layer that is currently implemented as a Box with a DarkGray background:\n`Box(modifier = Modifier.fillMaxSize().background(Color.DarkGray)) // Base simulated camera feed`\n\n3. THE FIX:\nReplace that specific mock Box with an `AndroidView` that uses `androidx.camera.view.PreviewView`. \n- Use `ProcessCameraProvider.getInstance(context)` to bind the `CameraSelector.DEFAULT_BACK_CAMERA` to the `LocalLifecycleOwner`.\n- Ensure the `Preview` use case is correctly linked to the `PreviewView.surfaceProvider`.\n\n4. PRESERVE OVERLAYS: \nCRITICAL: Do not alter or remove the `Column` containing the \"READY FOR INFERENCE PIPELINE\" bilingual text, nor the `Canvas` simulated viewfinder overlay below it. These must remain exactly as they are, layered perfectly on top of the new live CameraX feed.\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_START]\nSelected code path: /app/src/main/java/com/example/MainActivity.kt\nSelected line start: 480\nSelected line end: 480\nSelected code: CAMERA\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_END]"
    items {
      text: "Please update my Jetpack Compose project to replace the simulated mock camera feed with a real live camera feed using CameraX. \n\n1. DEPENDENCIES: \nOpen `app/build.gradle.kts` and add the following CameraX libraries to the dependencies block. Sync the project afterward:\nimplementation(\"androidx.camera:camera-camera2:1.3.1\")\nimplementation(\"androidx.camera:camera-lifecycle:1.3.1\")\nimplementation(\"androidx.camera:camera-view:1.3.1\")\n\n2. UI REFACTOR: \nIn my UI code, locate the `ScannerScreen` composable. Find the mock camera base layer that is currently implemented as a Box with a DarkGray background:\n`Box(modifier = Modifier.fillMaxSize().background(Color.DarkGray)) // Base simulated camera feed`\n\n3. THE FIX:\nReplace that specific mock Box with an `AndroidView` that uses `androidx.camera.view.PreviewView`. \n- Use `ProcessCameraProvider.getInstance(context)` to bind the `CameraSelector.DEFAULT_BACK_CAMERA` to the `LocalLifecycleOwner`.\n- Ensure the `Preview` use case is correctly linked to the `PreviewView.surfaceProvider`.\n\n4. PRESERVE OVERLAYS: \nCRITICAL: Do not alter or remove the `Column` containing the \"READY FOR INFERENCE PIPELINE\" bilingual text, nor the `Canvas` simulated viewfinder overlay below it. These must remain exactly as they are, layered perfectly on top of the new live CameraX feed.\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_START]\nSelected code path: /app/src/main/java/com/example/MainActivity.kt\nSelected line start: 480\nSelected line end: 480\nSelected code: CAMERA\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_END]"
